    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Expand $\\left(\\sqrt{x}-1+\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\right)^2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x-2\\sqrt{x}-\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}+\\dfrac{1}{x}+3$.\n\nExpand all products and collect like terms.",
      "worked": "For $x>0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\sqrt{x}-1+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\right)^2&=(\\sqrt{x})^2+(-1)^2+\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\right)^2+2(\\sqrt{x})(-1)+2\\sqrt{x}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}+2(-1)\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\\\\\left(\\sqrt{x}-1+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\right)^2&=x+1+\\frac{1}{x}-2\\sqrt{x}+2-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}\\\\\\left(\\sqrt{x}-1+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}}\\right)^2&=x-2\\sqrt{x}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{x}}+\\frac{1}{x}+3.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
